    "title": "public catch-cloth frame",
    "subject": "33019",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Current state",
        "text": "It shades the ground under it and the cells around it from the glare, for whoever stands there. You are standing in it.\nFair weather; the edge collects during mild showers. Shared catchment: 3/3 water available this interval. The frames share one allowance; missed rain is not stored."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How to use",
        "text": "Stand under it: it shades its own cell and the cells within 1 of it. During mild showers, stand beside the frame, press C and choose catch rain, then the exact carried flask or waterskin.\nNeeds: a compatible carried water vessel with room, and the intact public collecting edge.\nCost and limits: It only matters where the sun does: in the Beating at the Height of the day, bareheaded in the open you gain a stack of Parched every 10 turns, and under shade the count does not run. A hat or a roof does the same. Carried or taken up, it shades nothing. Both frames share three water per shower interval. This is optional water for existing uses; fair weather costs nothing.\nRight now you cannot: catch rain (There are no mild showers now. Ordinary water sources still work)."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Description",
        "text": "Waxed cloth on a fixed public frame gathers a little clean rainwater. Both frames share the allotment's catchment. During mild showers, press C here and choose a carried flask or waterskin. Ordinary water sources remain useful in fair weather."
      }
